Here is an example of a pseudocode and you might have seen this in your earlier

00:08:44.270 --> 00:08:53.350
courses also. What is this algorithm doing? This algorithm takes an array A which stores

00:08:53.350 --> 00:09:00.050
an integer in it and it is trying to find the maximum element in this array. What I have

00:09:00.050 --> 00:09:10.070
written here is not a program because I think the syntax is all wrong but it is a pseudocode.

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:17.750
It is a mixture of natural language and some high level programming constructs. I am going

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:22.290
to come to all of that but I am going to be using like a for, do, loop. I am going to use

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:26.870
